INT. VICTORIAN CONSERVATORY - AFTERNOON

Glass roof, iron ribs. Ferns the size of carriages. A wrought-iron table set for tea in the middle of a green jungle.

LADY EVELYN ASHCROFT (60s, lavender silk, a cane she uses more for pointing than walking) pours from a silver pot. Across from her, MR. JULIAN THORNBURY (30s, young solicitor, tight collar, too-new gloves) perches on the edge of a wicker chair.

EVELYN
Sugar, Mr. Thornbury?

JULIAN
Two, thank you.

EVELYN
Two. Ambitious.

JULIAN
I have a sweet tooth, Lady Ashcroft.

EVELYN
I have a lawyer's nephew with a sweet tooth. I trust you are not he.

JULIAN
I am nobody's nephew, my lady.

She drops two lumps. Stirs once. Hands the cup across.

EVELYN
Then you have no reason to flatter me.

JULIAN
I flatter no one.

EVELYN
A pity. I should like to be flattered. At my age it is the only vitamin.

He sips. Burns his tongue. Hides it.

JULIAN
My firm has sent me about the estate.

EVELYN
The estate.

JULIAN
The matter of the east orchard.

EVELYN
The orchard has been mine for forty years.

JULIAN
And the Hargreaves family wishes to purchase it.

EVELYN
The Hargreaves family wishes a great many things.

JULIAN
They offered considerably more than market value.

EVELYN
Then it is worth considerably more than market value.

JULIAN
(carefully)
That is what the firm suspects.

She sets down the pot. Studies him.

EVELYN
You are not as foolish as you dress.

JULIAN
I beg your pardon.

EVELYN
Nothing. Another biscuit?

JULIAN
Thank you.

He takes one. She watches him bite.

EVELYN
Do you know what grows in the east orchard, Mr. Thornbury?

JULIAN
Apples, I assume.

EVELYN
Apples. Pears. And beneath the fourth pear tree, a good deal else.

JULIAN
My lady?

EVELYN
Eat your biscuit.

He does. A parrot shrieks somewhere in the ferns. They both pretend not to hear it.

EVELYN (CONT'D)
My late husband was a collector.

JULIAN
Of what?

EVELYN
Whatever he could not bear to leave to others.

JULIAN
That is a poet's phrase.

EVELYN
He was not a poet.

A pause. The rain begins on the glass. Soft, then steady.

JULIAN
Is there anything I should tell the Hargreaves?

EVELYN
Tell them the orchard is not for sale.

JULIAN
May I tell them why?

EVELYN
You may tell them it is sentimental.

JULIAN
Is it?

EVELYN
Entirely.

JULIAN
I shall convey it.

She pours him more tea. They sit for a while without speaking.

JULIAN (CONT'D)
(gently)
Lady Ashcroft, the firm will not stop at one letter.

EVELYN
Then the firm will find me at home.

JULIAN
You are very brave.

EVELYN
I am very old. It is a different thing.

He smiles. She smiles back. In the glass, the rain keeps falling.

EVELYN (CONT'D)
Another cup, Mr. Thornbury?

JULIAN
Please.

She pours. The steam rises between them.
